# Force LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# SupplyGate ships committed sample artefacts (out/*.txt, out/*.json, and
# the sbom/ family). The compiler emits the SBOMs with LF on every OS, and
# the WASI backend writes the reports/gate JSON with LF too, so the only way
# a regenerated tree could differ from what ships here is a checkout that
# rewrote committed LF to CRLF (core.autocrlf). Every tracked file is text
# (.capa, .json, .txt, .md, .toml, .sh, LICENSE, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH); a
# blanket eol=lf is safe and keeps the reproducibility diff empty.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Reproducibility inputs, pinned LF for defence in depth.
sbom/SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH text eol=lf
generate.sh            text eol=lf
